From: EglantinePS5 <Vampinity@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: up: lean SSBO routing, global memory helpers kept as calls and routed by one switch (EDEN_UP_LEAN_SSBO)

What: when the shader translator cannot tie a native pointer access to one storage buffer, it
emits helper functions (loads, writes, atomics, compare-exchange) that pick the buffer at run time:
the closest base at or below the address, then one "if" per candidate buffer. Ocarina's foliage
compute programs have about 30 candidates and 40-odd such accesses, and a driver that inlines the
helpers copies that whole chain into every access. With EDEN_UP_LEAN_SSBO=1 the helpers are marked
DontInline (a hint to the driver: keep this a function call) and the per-buffer if-chain becomes
one OpSwitch (a jump on the chosen index). The bases, the choice, the accesses and the "no buffer"
fall-through are the same. The NVN size-word path (non-native pointers) is not changed.

Switches: EDEN_UP_LEAN_SSBO (read once). Exact "1": the lean code. Exact "2": the old code, plus the
count line (what 1 would route). Unset or anything else: the old code, byte for byte.
Log (stderr, mode 1 or 2, the first 400 programs with native routing, then every power of two):
"EDEN_UP_LEAN_SSBO mode M: program N (stage S[, mesh run as compute]), C candidate buffers,
H helper functions[ kept as calls], R routed|would be routed by one switch, A accesses through them".
Stage S is Shader::Stage (stage.h): 5 compute, 6 vertex A, 7 task, 8 mesh, 0-4 the other graphics
stages. A program with native routing and no storage buffer at all gets an OpSwitch with only a
default (valid SPIR-V, as upstream; the old code emitted no branch there).

Store stamp: it changes the emitted SPIR-V, so it is added to TranslationSwitches
(vk_pipeline_prep.cpp): kept translations (EDEN_UP_SHADER_PREP) made with and without it get
different stamps and never mix. Unset, the stamp is unchanged (only set names are mixed in). Mode 2
emits the old SPIR-V but, being set, gets a store of its own (harmless, a cold store for that arm).

Cost when off: per translated program with global memory, one cached static read and one counter
increment per helper function emitted (six or more per such program); nothing per draw, nothing in
the emitted code (the SPIR-V is byte for byte the old one).

Origin and credit: port of Djihads80/Eglantine 9a362357a2 by Duck912 (7 Nov 2026, branch nx2,
"spirv: keep native global memory helpers as calls and route with one switch"; there
EDEN_NX2_LEAN_SSBO, on by default). Both halves taken; the switch half was also ported as
javocsoft/Lichii 00a6bdd21 (not used here). Differences from upstream: our switch is off by default
and named EDEN_UP_; our compare-exchange helper (not in upstream) is DontInline too; mode 2 and
the count line are ours; it sits in the stamp; it adds #include <cstdio> for its line (upstream
added <cstdlib>, which ours already has). Upstream measured on NVIDIA only (first compile of
three foliage programs 2.4 s -> 0.6 s); the effect on RADV is not known.
Review fixes (review): this header's cost line (one increment per helper, not
two in all), the stage numbers, the include note and the zero-buffer edge case. Risk on the first =1
run: a driver that kept the calls and could not compile them would fail the foliage pipeline builds
(not draw them wrong); look for failed pipeline builds before reading any timing.
